{"uid":"modules/ai_fallback.py","name":"ai_fallback.py","qualname":"modules/ai_fallback.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/ai_fallback.py","line":1,"end_line":396,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"LazyOwn AI Fallback Chain ========================= Unified LLM caller with automatic fallback:","description":"1. Orchestrator chain (lazy_orchestrator pool, weight-sorted legs\n     executed through modules.llm_factory — groq, ollama, llamacpp,\n     pi, toposwarm)\n       ↓ when every chain member fails\n  2. Direct Groq call with the caller-supplied key (only when the chain\n     never attempted a groq leg)\n       ↓ on quota / rate-limit error\n  3. Ollama (local, requires ollama running + a chat model)\n       ↓ if Ollama unreachable or no suitable model\n  4. TopoSwarm local brain\n       ↓\n  5. Helpful error message with actionable steps\n\nUsed by recommender.py and timeline_narrator.py so fallback\nlogic lives in exactly one place.\n\nPublic API\n----------\ncall(prompt, system, api_key, max_tokens, temperature) -> AIResult\n\nAIResult fields:\n  .text     str   — the response text (or error/help message)\n  .backend  str   — \"groq\" | \"ollama\" | \"toposwarm\" | \"error\"\n  .model    str   — model name used\n  .error    str   — original error if fallback occurred (else \"\")","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/ai_fallback.py::AIResult","modules/ai_fallback.py::call"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
